WEBVTT

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:15.870
R-Robby...

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.750
Mr. Yang, you made it!

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.700
We all rolled up our sleeves
and reached the goal!

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.950
Yeah, but... we rolled up our
sleeves and reached the goal,

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.040
but Robby isn't here, is he?

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.160
What are you talking about, Mr. Yang?

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:35.370
Marathon relay races are the local
attraction on Planet Tottska.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:39.540
That doesn't mean that we
have to run, do we?

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:47.750
For crying out loud, anywhere we go,
it's "Isekandar," "Isekandar."

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:51.330
You're watching Galaxy Business Satellite.
Our next news story

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:55.540
concerns an elusive Odwarla oarfish
that was caught on Planet Odwarla.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:56.750
Ah! Mr. Yang!

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:58.500
It's them!

00:00:58.500 --> 00:00:59.950
What?!

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:05.580
I've found you, Robby. So, you
caught yourself a fish out there?

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.040
This time, I'm going to catch
a fish, too--namely, <i>you</i>.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:16.910
Space--the final tourist spot.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:20.660
There, we'll no doubt find epicurean
feats to stagger the imagination

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:25.660
and entirely new activities waiting for us!

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:46.120
"The hot springs planet Haccone"
"Hardly a very sophisticated name (heh)"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:47.450
"Will they be able to clear the galactic checkpoint?"
"The Don Opens All Doors"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar!
Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:51.000
"Will they be able to clear the galactic checkpoint?"
"The Don Opens All Doors"
♪ Let's go to Isekandar! ♪

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:54.620
It's coming into view!

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.000
Ho, that's it?

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.830
Galaxy Highway Checkpoint No. 1,
the Haccone Gateway.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.250
Wow! So this is the checkpoint?

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.700
The place sure is bustling, huh?

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.040
Over there.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.700
Huh? Hyperroad toll?

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.160
There's not just a transit fee,
but an expressway charge, too?

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:16.830
What choice do we have?

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:19.750
We can cover the distance that would take us

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.620
weeks at standard warp in no time at all.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:26.660
Wait, the money we got on Odwarla
will be all but used up, you know!

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.370
Isn't there any other way?

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:30.500
No, there isn't.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:34.910
This is the only hyperroad that connects
the galaxy to the rest of the universe.

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:39.330
Damn it, road concessions are all the same,
no matter which world you go to.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:42.000
Please show me your travel permits.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.660
Travel permits?

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.000
What are those?

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.540
Isn't a passport alone enough?

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:51.410
No. Lately, we have had an increase
in people leaving the galaxy illegally,

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:53.750
so they became mandatory as of April.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.370
I believe it was widely publicized.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.080
Seriously?

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:05.750
Damn it, I thought you were the type
who checks things out ahead of time.

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:08.450
<i>You </i>could stand to look into things
once in a while, yourself,

00:04:08.450 --> 00:04:10.250
Mr. Relies-on-others-for-everything.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:15.120
What?! So tell me, is food
the only thing you research?

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.870
You travel like a girl!

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:19.200
What's wrong with the way girls travel?

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.870
Now, now. For the time being,
let's stop on Planet Haccone

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:24.870
and figure out what we're going to do.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.370
Oh, it's a hot spring area!
I'm glad we made a stop at Haccone!

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.290
Oh, an alien fresh out of the waters!

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.950
Ooh, the back of her neck is out of this world!

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:42.620
Hurry up, let's go! Hot springs,
hot springs, hot springs!

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:47.950
There he goes. Best if we get out of here quick,
before he gets tricked again.

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:50.120
"Haccone's 10 most popular hot springs"

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:51.910
Which one should we choose?

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:53.910
Hatchi! Are you going
to the hot springs, too?!

00:04:55.700 --> 00:05:00.410
It really is like Earth's--or make that
Japan's hot springs, huh?

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:05.660
TripSunvisor said this was the most popular
hot spring and gave it five stars.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.870
Let's enjoy ourselves here for a bit.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:11.620
Yes! Hatchi, every once in a while,
we're on the same page.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:15.370
Come on, let's go. Hot springs, hot springs!
Mixed bathing with wet girls!

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:16.370
Well, I'm going, too.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:21.330
Hey, Hatchi! Have you sunk
to the same level that Robby has?

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:25.160
We're here anyway; might as well
enjoy the trip, right?

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:26.250
Huh?

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:31.200
From what I looked up, they can only
issue travel permits in one's homeland.

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.870
Huh? You mean, after all this,
we have to go back to Earth?

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:39.830
We can't do that. If I go back
to my homeland now...

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:42.500
But then, we'll work something out.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:43.950
Hot springs, hot springs!

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.370
H-Hey! Hatchi!

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.910
Jeez, they don't have mixed bathing?

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:56.620
You could learn a thing or two
from Edo-era culture!

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:00.830
I have to say, this is a melting pot for aliens.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:04.660
Wow, I'm impressed we managed
to score travel permits!

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:07.500
Shh! You're being too loud!

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.950
But then, that guy was really scary, huh?

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:15.410
Yeah. I'm never getting near
that guy again. It's too dangerous.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:20.160
Say, would you mind
telling me more about this?

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.080
What are you, in grade school?!

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:29.450
Shut up. You're a robot, so stop
being such a bossy pain in the ass,

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:30.830
you piece of junk!

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:34.250
I can't help it! Just look at who my owner is!

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:37.160
We might be able to get
our hands on travel permits!

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:38.500
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:41.410
What? Haccone's underworld boss?

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:44.040
Shh. We can't let anyone hear us.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:44.750
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.910
He also goes by the name
"The Schindler of Haccone."

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:50.750
Others call him "The Godfather of Haccone,"

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:55.580
"The Al Capone of Haccone," and even
"The Don Juan of Haccone."

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:58.540
Hey, that's laying it on pretty thick, isn't it?

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:00.500
Pick out your own character, why don't you?

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.540
So you're saying we don't have
to go all the way back to Earth?

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:08.080
That this underworld boss of Haccone
will issue us travel permits?

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:12.950
Yeah. But apparently, asking for
his help invites quite a bit of danger.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:14.080
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:16.700
There are those who have become
utterly hollowed-out husks,

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:19.080
and those who could never recover afterward.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.790
What's up with that?

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:24.080
But no one is willing to give out any specifics.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.870
That just proves how dangerous this guy is.

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:30.870
I'd also suspect whether or not the
travel permits he gives out are genuine.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:32.700
Suspect, nothing--

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:36.040
they're outright fakes! Anyone can tell that.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:40.040
No, apparently, they aren't.

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:43.040
The travel permits he gives out
are said to carry even more weight

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:46.000
than the ones you get from your homeland.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:50.410
You get treated on a whole different
level just by carrying one.

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:55.410
What, like a black card? Or more like
Mito Komon's lacquered case?

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:59.540
Isn't that just because of
how scary this guy is, though?

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:04.950
Like he's the dark emperor that
rules the universe? Scary stuff!

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:06.910
Can I get some more sake over here?

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:08.160
Sure, kappa.

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:08.870
--And maybe I should top you off, too.

00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:10.790
--So, how are you planning to get
travel permits out of this guy?
--And maybe I should top you off, too.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.120
--So, how are you planning to get
travel permits out of this guy?
--Ah, sir, kappa!

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:12.910
--So, how are you planning to get
travel permits out of this guy?
--A little <i>kanpai </i>for the kappa!

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:15.450
--In any case, it's worth going to have a look.
--A little <i>kanpai </i>for the kappa!

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.660
--Here?
--Here?

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:21.500
There's what appear
to be black egg gatekeepers.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:25.910
I've never seen anyone so round,
yet so terrifying.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.830
H-Help us!

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:31.370
Hey, what's the matter?
What happened to you?

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:34.080
H-He's an absolute horror show!

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.120
Horror show?

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:37.200
I was afraid he was going
to leave me an empty shell!

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:40.330
That's somebody you should
never go anywhere near!

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:42.950
Are you talking about the
underworld boss of Haccone?

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:45.250
Th-The truth is...

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:50.290
He really does sound dangerous, all right.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:53.450
Hey, Hatchi, are you serious about seeing him?

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:55.790
Maybe we should come up with a plan first.

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:57.120
Excuse me!

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:58.870
--Huh?!
--Huh?!

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:02.910
I'd like to see the person in charge here.

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:04.580
That idiot!

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:06.620
Wh-What are you doing?

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:09.200
Look, I'm sorry about the kid, here.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:11.200
We'll just take him away, right now.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:17.040
This is nothing to laugh at!

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:21.660
But I mean, a grown man and a robot
groveling before black eggs!

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:25.000
That's hilarious! Groveling before black eggs!

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.330
Now, look! If we hadn't done something,

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:30.790
we would have come <i>this </i>close
to having our souls sucked out!

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:32.830
So hilarious!

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:35.620
This guy's seriously twisted.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:37.660
Here you go.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:40.910
Huh? Is this coffee?

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:45.160
It's one of Haccone's local delicacies--
peach hot spring coffee.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:48.160
Peach? That's shocking pink.

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:51.870
Incidentally, it gets 4.7 stars on TripSunvisor.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:56.450
The comments say it's great together
with peach hot spring <i>manju </i>buns.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:10:00.870
Listen to you. You never looked up
something as critical as transit permits,

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:04.950
but you check out something like <i>this</i>.
You really do travel like a girl.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:08.080
Oh! It tastes just like regular coffee!

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:11.700
Yummy!

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:17.950
What are we going to do, though?
We can't stay around here forever.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:22.450
We'll run out of money to pay for the
checkpoint fees and hyperroad toll.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:25.870
Okay, Ikku, you can just pop
back to Earth by yourself

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:28.660
and get our transit passes for us.

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:31.500
We'll be here enjoying the
hot springs in the meantime.

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:32.910
Huh?!

00:10:32.910 --> 00:10:36.500
Robots can't go in the
hot springs anyway, right?

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.500
Why, you...!

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.790
Oh! What perfect timing!

00:10:40.790 --> 00:10:43.500
All those pretty girls in their yukatas,
right out of the baths!

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:46.830
Well, I'm off to go enjoy
the hot springs with them.

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:49.000
Ikku, we're counting on you.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.910
Hey there, are you all here on vacation?

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:54.250
Come on, Robby! Damn that idiot.

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.450
Hey! Is this any time to be so relaxed?!

00:10:56.450 --> 00:11:00.120
Never mind him, what really concerns me...

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:01.790
...is the barkeeper.

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:03.000
Huh?

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:06.620
Shh. While he's been toweling off those cups,

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:08.950
he's been eavesdropping on us.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:13.450
I'm sure he's connected
to the underworld boss.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:24.330
So how exactly is he able
to collect information?

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:25.910
Thank you very much.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.830
Not at all.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:29.540
Did you find anything out?

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:31.790
Yeah. Come on, let's go.

00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:37.290
So, where should we go next?

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:39.040
It's time to hit the hot springs, right?

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:41.620
The open-air baths, right? Right?

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:44.040
Huh, what should we do?

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:46.830
Why don't we get some
hot spring shave ice, instead?

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:49.700
They say they make it
with natural Haccone ice.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:52.120
I'm in! Oh, and I want some <i>yuba-don</i>, too.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:54.330
Let's go on the Udenoko Lake pirate ship, too.

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:56.660
--Yeah! Yeah!
--Yeah! Yeah!

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:07.080
What gives, Hatchi? Do you want
to go on the pirate ship?

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:11.580
That barkeeper back there really
does know the underworld boss.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:12.660
Huh?

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:15.950
His daughter apparently fell victim to him.

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:18.790
She now works at the ticket counter here.

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:22.870
I'm surprised the barkeeper would
tell you something like that.

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:25.450
Come on, let's go, let's go.

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:28.450
Hatchi's skipping may
appear to be free of care,

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:31.870
but it scares me in a different
sense than Robby does.

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:34.410
Um, excuse me...

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.080
I hope you won't mind me asking this, but--

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:39.040
Oh, you're here, too, are you?

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:39.910
Huh?

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:41.620
Robby!

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:43.580
Hey, is that boy your friend, Robby?

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:48.290
Not so much "friend" as "underling."
His name's Hatchi.

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:49.870
He's so cute!

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:52.160
Hatchi is such a hottie!

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:55.250
Hey, Hatchi, let's take a picture together!

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:59.620
Huh? Uh... um... I mean...

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:02.580
These turned out amazing!

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:05.580
Hey, Hatchi, let's go on
the pirate ship together!

00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:07.580
N-No, I need to...

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.200
Oh, come with us!

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.750
Let's go, let's go!

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:13.620
--What tremendous girl-like traveling power.
--I happen to have four tickets right here!

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:16.620
Hey, wait! What about me?!

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:18.450
Damn that Hatchi!

00:13:18.450 --> 00:13:21.830
He took all of my tourist girls away from me!

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:25.250
I mean, why Hatchi and not <i>me</i>?!

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:28.200
Tourist girls aren't interested in older men.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.250
You take a lousy picture, too.

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:35.580
They're too young to understand
the appeal of a grown-up.

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:38.580
The greatest appeal of
a grown-up is typically money.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:43.620
In that regard, you have zero appeal.
In fact, make that negative.

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:46.580
But I came all the way here from Earth!

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:48.120
Excuse me...

00:13:49.450 --> 00:13:52.200
Did you say you were from Earth?

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:58.000
Huh? Yes, I am... What is it?
Are you interested in me?

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:01.290
You Earth men really do love
your hot springs, don't you?

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:05.870
Oh, am I to understand that your
last boyfriend was from Earth?

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:11.200
Oh, no. The person who
got me this job loves Earth

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:13.580
and often spoke about its hot springs.

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:16.870
Oh, yeah? Then what do you say

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:20.040
I continue telling you about them over
in those lakeside open-air baths?

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:24.120
Ah! I was just thinking of stopping by
there on the way home from work.

00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:27.830
--By all means.
--Yes! Time for an older man to shine!

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:29.790
Hey! Robby!

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:33.750
Man! Hatchi and those tourist girls
are on the pirate ship!

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:36.040
Aw, I can't take this!

00:14:39.700 --> 00:14:43.580
Sheesh, it's not mixed bathing here, either?

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:45.080
The water is nice, isn't it?

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:45.950
Huh?

00:14:45.950 --> 00:14:49.660
It is, it is. And the view
of the lake is nice, too.

00:14:49.660 --> 00:14:53.540
As it happens, my benefactor
is the one who built this hot spring.

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:55.160
Oh, yeah?

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:59.580
Ah, so <i>that's </i>the dumb bastard
that didn't make this mixed bathing.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:03.250
So, have you been to the
Kappappa Hot Springs?

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:05.330
Yeah, I have, I have.

00:15:05.330 --> 00:15:08.540
My benefactor built that facility, too.

00:15:08.540 --> 00:15:12.290
He's the man who brought
hot springs to this world.

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:13.580
Oh, yeah?

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:18.950
Hey, man, if you're making that
much money, build a mixed bath, too.

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:21.910
Ugh, I'm exhausted.

00:15:21.910 --> 00:15:25.620
Welcome back. How was it? Enjoy yourself?

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:27.450
I'm more interested in where Robby is.

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:31.040
Ah, he went gallivanting off to the hot springs

00:15:31.040 --> 00:15:33.080
with the girl from the ticket counter.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:33.910
Huh?

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:37.540
Hey, Hatchi, come to the hot springs with us!

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:39.700
Oh, no, I really need to...

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.080
Come on, come on, let's go!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.250
Ikku, help me!

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:49.910
See if I care! Damn Robby and Hatchi both
for dallying around the hot springs!

00:15:49.910 --> 00:15:53.000
Robby, I'm going to head on out.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:57.500
Oh, yeah, I should be on my way, too. Huh...?

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:58.870
Hatchi, you're here, too?

00:15:58.870 --> 00:16:01.330
Ah, yeah, well...

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:04.080
Wow, open-air baths!

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:05.500
Amazing!

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:06.330
--The view here is fantastic!

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:11.620
--It's those girls from earlier!
Maybe I <i>will </i>stay in a little longer.
--The view here is fantastic!

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:17.500
Cut it out, would you, grown-up?

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:23.290
Where's the harm? It's a boundless,
sound-only, uncensored world!

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:27.200
I'm free to imagine for myself what's happening.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:32.000
Never mind that, I heard something from Ikku.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:35.160
Did you come here with the girl
from the ticket counter?

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:39.910
Yeah, I did. Turns out this hot spring,
the huge one earlier,

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:45.790
and all the hot springs on this world
were built by Kapako's benefactor.

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:48.950
Could that mean... Where is she?!

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:52.410
She was over in the women's bath
up until a moment ago.

00:16:58.040 --> 00:16:59.540
What are you doing?!

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:01.330
Well, my information on the underworld boss--

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:04.450
Shut up! Although, that was a bit lucky...

00:17:04.450 --> 00:17:06.870
Still, Kapako wasn't over there anymore.

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:08.870
Uh, Kapako!

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:11.410
Hey! Don't leave me behind!

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:20.160
Kapako!

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:27.870
You're Kapako, daughter of barkeeper
at the teahouse, right?

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:30.660
Y-Yes...

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:35.120
I heard from your father about
what happened with <i>that </i>man.

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:40.580
How, for a time, you were hurt so badly
that you weren't just left empty,

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:42.330
but fractured, as well.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:45.160
"Hurt" isn't how I would put it...

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.750
I realize the past may be painful for you,

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:53.040
but I really need you to tell me about <i>him</i>.

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:56.370
We have to get past the checkpoint,
whatever it takes!

00:17:56.370 --> 00:18:02.000
We need his help to do that.
We need him to issue us transit permits.

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:06.870
Please, tell me how we can
get him to cooperate with us!

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:08.540
Hatchi...

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:13.000
He will probably be willing
to give you transit permits.

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:14.080
Huh?

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:19.290
But I've never heard of anyone who has
met him and remained unaffected.

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:21.500
Is he really that dangerous?

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:25.120
He is the person who has the
most love in the whole universe.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:29.000
It's just that the power of that love
is extremely strong.

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.500
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:35.000
If you really do go to meet him,
as long as you don't look right at him,

00:18:35.000 --> 00:18:38.200
you may be able to avoid
that risk to some extent.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:39.540
So, don't...

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:41.290
...look directly at him?

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:46.160
We want you to take us to your boss.

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:48.540
Are you sure you're ready to do so?

00:18:48.540 --> 00:18:50.370
Of course! Right?

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:53.580
I'm scared, but what other choice is there?

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:58.500
I've got nothing to hollow out
or fracture, so I'll be okay!

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:00.790
All right, go ahead.

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:11.370
There's no one here.

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:15.660
Ah! There's someone over there!

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:28.700
Guys, do as you were told,
and don't look directly at him!

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:30.370
Yeah, we know.

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:32.160
Yeah.

00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:34.870
Is there something I can do for you?

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:40.410
Yes, um, I hope this day
finds you well, and, um...

00:19:40.410 --> 00:19:42.790
Hey, Robby! Keep it together!

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:47.160
I'll come right to it. Would you
be willing to offer us your help

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:49.120
by issuing us travel permits?

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:51.660
Travel permits?

00:19:53.290 --> 00:19:55.660
Guys, be sure not to look.

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:56.750
Yeah.

00:19:58.950 --> 00:20:01.500
Hey, Hatchi! Did you hear me?!

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:15.950
H-Hey! No, Hatchi!

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:17.910
What are you two doing?!

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:23.660
A pink...

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:25.200
...wombat?

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:28.410
If that's all you need, I can take care of it.

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:33.040
The universe is filled with love!

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:36.000
Love power!

00:20:50.910 --> 00:20:53.830
He is a dangerous man, all right.

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:59.410
Once a person is caught up in all his
vast love, they become captivated!

00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:01.870
Not to mention how dangerously fluffy he is.

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:04.580
They won't be able to live
without his fluffiness.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:08.660
No wonder it leaves them
hollowed out and fractured!

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:11.870
Although, I'm a robot,
so it doesn't matter to me.

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:16.250
Anyhow, we safely got these issued
to us, so everything's fine.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:19.040
Please show me your travel permits.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:20.950
--Here!
--Here!

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:22.700
Th-That mark!

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:25.330
Let's see... Here! Take a complimentary

00:21:25.330 --> 00:21:30.000
"Anytime, Anywhere,
Fluffy Cellphone Strap of Love."

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.540
Th-Thanks...

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:37.700
We're all on our way to Isekandar. Off we go!

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:41.950
Why do they get to pass
without having travel permits?

00:21:41.950 --> 00:21:46.200
You don't know? The Space Tourism
Administration issued a notice

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:48.790
that visitors to Isekandar
have special permission

00:21:48.790 --> 00:21:52.870
to pass without any travel permits.

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:54.660
--Huh?!
--Huh?!

00:22:02.950 --> 00:22:06.040
<i>Nagaya Voyager</i>, you are cleared to proceed.

00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:12.910
Yes! Go, <i>Nagaya Voyager</i>! Isekandar or bust!

00:22:12.910 --> 00:22:15.620
Like I said, that's really not necessary.

00:23:51.950 --> 00:23:52.870
"Next time"
"#06 'Qu-eel-le Surprise'"

00:23:52.870 --> 00:23:56.950
"Next time"
"#06 'Qu-eel-le Surprise'"
Next time, "Qu-eel-le Surprise."

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:01.910
"The local delicacy of
Planet Hamama II is space eel"
"The Great Eel Festival is underway!"

00:24:02.080 --> 00:24:06.950
"Did you think 'It's the Day of the Ox,
so why are they doing eels?'"
"You didn't? In that case, excuse me.
Ah, I'd like some broiled eel."
